## Code Standards

<!-- Non-negotiable coding standards for this project -->

### Style
- [ ] Prettier for formatting
- [ ] ESLint config from `eslint.config.js`
- [ ] TypeScript strict mode enabled
- [ ] Prefer `const` over `let`; never use `var`

### Patterns
- [ ] REST API responses follow: `{ data, error, meta }` shape
- [ ] All async functions must handle errors explicitly
- [ ] No `any` types without an accompanying `// eslint-disable` with reason

### Naming
- [ ] Components: PascalCase (`UserProfile.tsx`)
- [ ] Files: kebab-case (`user-profile.tsx`)
- [ ] Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE
- [ ] Booleans start with `is`, `has`, `can`

---

## Commands

<!-- Standard commands for this project. Claude will use these when asked to run tests, build, etc. -->

```bash
# Development
npm run dev          # Start dev server
npm run lint         # Run linter
npm run typecheck    # TypeScript check

# Testing
npm test             # Run all tests
npm run test:watch   # Watch mode
npm run test:coverage # Coverage report

# Build & Deploy
npm run build        # Production build
npm run start        # Start production server
```

---

## Directory Structure

```
src/
├── app/              # Next.js App Router pages
├── components/       # Reusable UI components
├── lib/              # Utilities and helpers
├── server/           # Server-side code (API routes, actions)
└── types/            # TypeScript type definitions
```

---

## Subagents Usage

<!-- Which subagents to invoke for what -->

- `@architect-planner`: New features, refactoring decisions
- `@backend-dev`: API endpoints, server logic
- `@frontend-dev`: React components, UI implementation
- `@db-schema-expert`: Prisma schema changes, migrations
- `@security-auditor`: Auth flows, user data handling
- `@test-runner`: Test authoring, coverage improvements
- `@code-reviewer`: Pre-PR review
- `@devops-engineer`: Deploy config, CI/CD

---

## Constraints

<!-- Things Claude should NEVER do in this project -->

- [ ] Never commit `.env` files
- [ ] Never use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without review
- [ ] Never bypass authentication middleware
- [ ] Never run migrations directly on production
- [ ] Never disable TypeScript errors without justification

